[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Benoni Defense"]
[Variation "Benoni Defense: Old Benoni"]
[ECO "A43"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "space-advantage,d5-wedge"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "1...c5"]
[Start "orthodox 1.d4"]

1... c5 2. d5 { Against 1...c5 the bishop on f4 can be hit by ...cxd4 and ...Qb6 ideas, so White grabs space instead. The pawn on d5 cramps Black's pieces. } 2... Nf6 ( 2... e6 3. c4 exd5 ( 3... Nf6 4. Nc3 ) ( 3... d6 4. Nc3 ) 4. cxd5 { Recaptures towards the centre. The pawn on d5 still cramps Black. } 4... d6 ( 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 ) 5. Nc3 ) ( 2... e5 3. e4 d6 ( 3... Nf6 4. Nc3 ) 4. Nc3 ) ( 2... d6 3. e4 Nf6 ( 3... e6 4. Nc3 ) ( 3... e5 4. Nc3 ) ( 3... g6 4. Nc3 ) 4. Nc3 { Transposes to 2...Nf6 3.Nc3 d6 4.e4. } ) 3. Nc3 d6 ( 3... e6 4. e4 ) ( 3... g6 4. e4 ) ( 3... Qa5 4. Bd2 ) 4. e4 { Builds a big centre. Black can only hit it with ...e6 or ...b5, and neither breaks it easily. } 4... g6 ( 4... Bg4 5. Nf3 ) ( 4... e5 5. Nf3 ) ( 4... Qa5 5. Bd2 ) 5. Nf3 Bg7 6. Be2 { Gets the king ready to castle and keeps the e4 pawn solid. } 6... O-O 7. O-O { King safe. The pawns on d5 and e4 stop Black's pieces: aim for Bf4 or Bg5, Nd2 and f4 or a quiet queenside. } *
